; Dungeons of Daggorath -- P17 M1: the dungeon and the view, and M2: the
; command line and the clock.
;
;   load "daggorath
;   daggorath
;
; docs/daggorath-design.md is the design; this file is M1 and M2's slice of
; it -- section 15: M1 is "the cell walk, the architectural lists, MOVE and
; TURN with both animations, the grey ramp, the inverted levels including
; the status bar, and hw.setcpu "fast with restore.clock behind it"; M2 is
; "the scheduler of section 5, the parser (PARSER.ASM/TOKEN.ASM), the text
; furniture of sections 4.1b-4.1c, the heart drawn and beating, fainting,
; damage recovery, death."
;
; This file does NOT include (each is a later milestone by design section
; 15):
;   - objects, the bag, both hands, torches and the two light channels
;     (M3) -- the status line names both hands, but nothing ever puts
;     anything in one, so both read EMPTY (STATUS.ASM's own M$EMPT), and
;     the fade reads off a fixed ambient light (`dagg.light`) rather than
;     RLIGHT from a burning torch.
;   - creatures, peeks, combat (M4) -- no CFIND/PDRAW, and no LUKNEW in
;     the scheduler because nothing sets NEWLUK yet.
;   - ladders/holes/VFTTAB (M5) -- the forward view always draws the plain
;     ceiling line (VERT.ASM:CELINE).
;   - sound (M6) -- the heart beats and is drawn, but the thump on voices
;     0 and 4 (design section 9.4) is M6's.
;   - thirteen of the fifteen commands, which is why `dagg.soon` exists:
;     MOVE and TURN are the two this file can already act on.
;
; The maze and the architectural vector lists are generated into this file
; by scripts/gen_daggorath.py -- see the marked block below. There is no
; second file to ship and nothing to open at run time.

;==========================================================================
; The scale tables -- design section 6.1, verbatim (also tests/logo/p17m0,
; where the transform this file reuses was board-confirmed at M0).

make "dagg.norscl [200 128 80 50 31 20 12 8 4 2]
make "dagg.hlfscl [255 156 100 65 40 26 16 10 6 3]

; BAKSCL, VIEWER.ASM: "the same table shifted one entry along" -- the
; second through eleventh entries of the eleven-value HLFSCL/BAKSCL block
; VIEWER.ASM lays out (the eleventh, marked *DEBUG in the source, is
; BAKSCL's own last entry, not dead data once the table is read this way).
make "dagg.bakscl [156 100 65 40 26 16 10 6 3 1]

; VECTOR.ASM's fade table (design section 8), the dash column -- P18 M2's
; `setpendash` makes a dotted stroke cost the same as a solid one, so dots
; are M1's default (the grey alternative is M1a, optional, not built here).
;
; It is BITMSK read through two of VECTOR.ASM's own quirks. SETFAX loads
; `BITMSK+8` indexed by A, and A only ever reaches -6 there (the `CMPA #-7
; / BLE` above it takes the darkness branch first), so the six entries used
; are BIT0 through BIT5 -- 1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32. VECTOR then does `INC
; VCTFAD` before loading FADCNT from it, so the PERIOD is one more than the
; table byte: 2, 3, 5, 9, 17, 33. There is no 65 -- design section 8 lists
; one, reading BITMSK as though A reached -7, and that entry is unreachable
; because -7 is already total darkness.
make "dagg.dash [1 2 3 5 9 17 33]

; No torches yet (M3), so the fade reads off a fixed ambient light rather
; than RLIGHT -- 8, "typical dungeon level 1 or 2" per VIEWER.ASM's own
; comment on the RLIGHT input. A placeholder, not a guess dressed up as one.
make "dagg.light 8

;==========================================================================
; The maze and the architectural vector lists.
;
; EVERYTHING BETWEEN THE TWO MARKERS BELOW IS GENERATED. Do not hand-edit
; it -- run `python3 scripts/gen_daggorath.py`, which rewrites the block in
; place (and gates the mazes against docs/DungeonsOfDaggorath/Levels/).
;
; It is *in this file* rather than in a `daggdata` beside it because a game
; should be one file to ship. That costs nothing in RAM: measured on the
; host, whole-row list literals land in exactly the same node and word-table
; count `readlist` did (27,082 free nodes against 27,025, the difference
; being the loader procedure that no longer exists). What it does cost is
; the 40-column source rule -- a maze row is 32 numbers and will not fit,
; and splitting it into 40-column pieces to be reassembled with `se` is the
; one form that is NOT free: that burns ~10,900 word-table entries where
; the whole-row literal burns none.
;
; Mazes are a list of levels of 32 rows of 32 cells, not flattened -- see
; dagg.cell. Each vector list is a list of runs, and each run is already
; the two parallel ys/xs lists `dagg.draw.run` wants: the generator does
; the splitting section 6.3 used to do here at load time, which is why
; `dagg.ys.of`, `dagg.xs.of` and `dagg.read.runs` are gone.

